  "raw": " in a bid to prevent the United States from sliding deeper into an economic recession.\n\n\"Let me be clear: I don't want to go into a fiscal cliff. I don't want to see us slip back into an economic depression,\" Lew said in an interview with CBS's \"Face the Nation.\" If an agreement is not reached to raise the U.S. debt limit, the government would likely stop borrowing for a while starting in early November, which would shut off the government's ability to pay its bills.\n\nAs one of the few remaining bright spots during this year, the U.S. economy has struggled to take off amid weak consumer demand, tepid business spending, tepid housing activity and an ailing government, which took a hit from the government shutdown earlier in the summer.\n\nLew also warned the U.S. Congress against using the economy's shaky state as a stick with which to compel lawmakers to vote up or down on a pending increase",
  "serialized": "in a bid to prevent the United States from sliding deeper into an economic recession. \"Let me be clear: I don't want to go into a fiscal cliff. I don't want to see us slip back into an economic depression,\" Lew said in an interview with CBS's \"Face the Nation.\" If an agreement is not reached to raise the U.S. debt limit, the government would likely stop borrowing for a while starting in early November, which would shut off the government's ability to pay its bills. As one of the few remaining bright spots during this year, the U.S. economy has struggled to take off amid weak consumer demand, tepid business spending, tepid housing activity and an ailing government, which took a hit from the government shutdown earlier in the summer. Lew also warned the U.S. Congress against using the economy's shaky state as a stick with which to compel lawmakers to vote up or down on a pending increase",
